{"name":"Hearts of Palm","hex":"#cfc291","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hearts of palm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of heart of palm"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearts_of_palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heart of palm","blocks":[{"text":"Heart of palm is a vegetable harvested from the inner core and growing bud of certain palm trees, most notably the coconut, juçara, açaí palm, palmetto, and peach palm. Heart of palm may be eaten on its own, and often it is eaten in a salad. Hearts of palm are traditionally harvested in the cultures of Southeast Asia and in South and Central America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Heart_of_palm.jpg/330px-Heart_of_palm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_of_palm","wikidata":"Q743144"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg/500px-9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg/1280px-9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg/500px-9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Julienned ubod (coconut heart) from the Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A9850Foods_Fruits_Baliuag_Bulacan_Philippines_18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Ubod_kan_niyog.jpg/500px-Ubod_kan_niyog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb